1
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:07,140
In my life, I've killed 13 people.

2
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:16,880
Compared to the average idiot,
I think I'm pretty strong.

3
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:22,850
Killing is fun.

4
00:00:25,180 --> 00:00:29,940
The look on the face of
that posturing jarl's brat...

5
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,610
That's how I know.

6
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:40,970
This row of enemies in front of me...

7
00:00:50,780 --> 00:00:53,340
I'm scared! I'm scared, I'm scared...

8
00:00:53,340 --> 00:00:56,920
But damn it... they're enjoying this.

9
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:13,080
Fuck!

10
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:18,900
Gudmund!

11
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,330
M-My legs...

12
00:01:26,630 --> 00:01:30,190
Ah, they're going to kill Badger.

13
00:01:30,470 --> 00:01:32,790
I don't believe it.

14
00:01:32,790 --> 00:01:36,190
How's he able to get so close
to the Jomsvikings?

15
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:48,910
Boss?

16
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:52,750
Fox, take Badger and fall back to the fort!

17
00:01:55,600 --> 00:01:58,550
All forces, retreat!

18
00:01:58,550 --> 00:02:00,970
Re—?! You can't be serious!

19
00:02:00,970 --> 00:02:02,550
I can still fight!

20
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:06,260
Enough, Badger! Look around you!

21
00:02:06,740 --> 00:02:12,260
Damn it. Did all these men have to die for him
to know how much stronger the enemy is?

22
00:02:13,270 --> 00:02:16,020
Retreat!

23
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:17,740
What? Retreat?

24
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:19,650
All right!

25
00:02:21,650 --> 00:02:24,910
Don't bunch up! Spread out and flee!

26
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:27,540
Wait for me! My legs...

27
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:33,500
Retreat? I didn't order a retreat!

28
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:38,290
Where's your honor?
And you call yourself Norse men!

29
00:02:38,290 --> 00:02:39,830
W-Wait up!

30
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,390
I told you not to run.

31
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,520
You think I'll forgive your debt after this?

32
00:02:53,700 --> 00:02:58,020
Debt? Either way,
you're finished, Mister Ketil.

33
00:03:00,170 --> 00:03:05,450
Do you understand what
it's like to be poor like us now?

34
00:03:06,510 --> 00:03:12,840
No matter how unfair it may be,
you shouldn't defy the king.

35
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:17,710
It's the same reason we've
always listened to you!

36
00:03:18,990 --> 00:03:22,320
Might makes right, Mister Ketil.

37
00:03:22,950 --> 00:03:28,790
The world exists for people
stronger than you.

38
00:03:37,090 --> 00:03:37,980
They're here!

39
00:03:48,950 --> 00:03:50,500
What is it, Wulf?

40
00:03:49,450 --> 00:03:55,120
Pain

41
00:03:50,900 --> 00:03:52,540
Ah, Your Majesty.

42
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:57,800
Someone who may have been Ketil
was just defeated by one of my men.

43
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:03,050
How inept. My orders were to capture him.

44
00:04:03,480 --> 00:04:06,820
Yes, Your Majesty. I apologize.

45
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:08,680
I'll go confirm what happened.

46
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:12,710
The Jomsvikings are attacking
the backs of the fleeing soldiers.

47
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:14,640
That goes against my orders as well.

48
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,500
Tell Floki not to pursue them.

49
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:18,370
Yes, Your Majesty.

50
00:04:30,300 --> 00:04:33,120
I'm not sure why,
but his guard captain left his side.

51
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:35,830
This is my chance.

52
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:43,140
Treat the bodies with care.

53
00:04:43,140 --> 00:04:44,880
We'll return them to their families—

54
00:04:50,190 --> 00:04:55,890
King Canute, your head is mine!

55
00:06:38,030 --> 00:06:40,220
Th-Thorgil!

56
00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:42,090
Where'd you come from?

57
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:46,400
From Helheim.

58
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:52,780
I'm surprised.

59
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:55,740
I didn't think you could block my swing.

60
00:06:55,740 --> 00:06:58,640
Your skills have improved, Your Majesty.

61
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:01,890
My right hand feels weak.

62
00:07:02,720 --> 00:07:05,150
Did that single blow sprain it?

63
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:06,960
Good.

64
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:10,530
You're a commander worth killing.

65
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:30,710
I wish we had time to play,
but I'm in a hurry.

66
00:07:31,190 --> 00:07:35,220
Your head is mine.

67
00:07:49,630 --> 00:07:53,490
Bastard! How dare you kick the king!

68
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:06,280
Die!

69
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:21,660
Your Majesty, give your sword to me.

70
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:22,930
Please stand back.

71
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:26,150
Damn it.

72
00:08:30,350 --> 00:08:32,340
King's guard, fall back!

73
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:34,490
Defend the king!

74
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:41,280
Damn it!

75
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:43,450
Stop, Thorgil!

76
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:46,810
Don't pursue him too far, Wulf.

77
00:08:46,810 --> 00:08:48,710
You're seriously injured as well.

78
00:08:49,890 --> 00:08:55,840
I let my guard down,
but more than that, he's a bold man.

79
00:08:57,150 --> 00:08:59,400
I wish he'd serve me again.

80
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:03,930
King's guard, fall back!

81
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:06,980
His Majesty is under attack!

82
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:09,060
All forces, fall back!

83
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:12,260
Run! Hurry!

84
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,440
Your Majesty!

85
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,980
Your Majesty!

86
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:17,640
Wh-What's going on?

87
00:09:18,370 --> 00:09:22,200
Who would do something like that?
Was it Thorgil?

88
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:27,960
That was close.

89
00:09:32,670 --> 00:09:35,050
Master, are you alive?

90
00:09:39,230 --> 00:09:40,300
Okay.

91
00:09:40,980 --> 00:09:46,350
Looks like those soldiers
didn't recognize you.

92
00:09:46,350 --> 00:09:48,310
You're a lucky man.

93
00:09:49,740 --> 00:09:51,810
Damn heavy, too.

94
00:09:54,540 --> 00:09:58,320
Don't think you can get off easy by dying.

95
00:09:59,200 --> 00:10:06,390
You have responsibilities as the
losing force's leader, Iron Fist Ketil.

96
00:10:23,540 --> 00:10:25,830
I hear it...

97
00:10:30,700 --> 00:10:36,880
The sound I heard when my village burned.

98
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:42,920
The sound of the world falling apart.

99
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:49,960
They're fighting, aren't they?

100
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:54,500
It's all right. Don't worry.

101
00:10:55,360 --> 00:10:57,410
We aren't slaves anymore.

102
00:10:58,060 --> 00:11:00,040
We're leaving this farm.

103
00:11:01,410 --> 00:11:06,120
That battle has nothing to do with us.

104
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:16,060
Where will we go once we leave this place?

105
00:11:20,050 --> 00:11:21,940
We can go to my village.

106
00:11:23,470 --> 00:11:26,740
It's a bit cold, but it's a nice place.

107
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:34,820
Do you have slaves there?

108
00:11:36,620 --> 00:11:41,060
Do you have wars?

109
00:11:43,900 --> 00:11:48,230
Yes. Battles were fought there once.

110
00:11:48,770 --> 00:11:52,850
I'd be lying if I said
it would never happen again.

111
00:11:56,830 --> 00:12:00,240
I'm not going.

112
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:06,360
I'm going somewhere else.

113
00:12:08,830 --> 00:12:12,820
Gardar and the children...

114
00:12:16,670 --> 00:12:19,780
are waiting for me.

115
00:12:22,190 --> 00:12:26,100
I just wanted to express my gratitude.

116
00:12:31,010 --> 00:12:36,760
Thank you, Einar and Thorfinn.

117
00:12:38,660 --> 00:12:40,640
Thank you.

118
00:12:46,080 --> 00:12:56,080
I felt like I was wandering through
a terrible nightmare all alone.

119
00:13:00,140 --> 00:13:01,570
But...

120
00:13:09,970 --> 00:13:13,430
Our morning chats...

121
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:21,350
I enjoyed your stories, Einar...

122
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:26,190
No, Arnheid!

123
00:13:26,820 --> 00:13:29,720
Hang in there, Arnheid!

124
00:13:30,750 --> 00:13:32,440
Arnheid!

125
00:13:33,950 --> 00:13:39,790
Didn't you say you'd protect
the child inside you?

126
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:42,180
Arnheid!

127
00:13:48,060 --> 00:13:52,300
The child has already gone
to the other side.

128
00:13:59,650 --> 00:14:01,720
They're all dead.

129
00:14:03,490 --> 00:14:06,310
All of my loved ones.

130
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:12,360
What point is there in going on living?

131
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:19,760
There's nothing left for me here.

132
00:14:22,550 --> 00:14:26,390
Why do I have to live?

133
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:38,220
I... Because... Because I...

134
00:14:43,170 --> 00:14:45,900
Arnheid? Arnheid?

135
00:14:46,590 --> 00:14:47,900
Arnheid!

136
00:14:47,900 --> 00:14:49,840
Move, Einar!

137
00:14:54,450 --> 00:14:59,920
My father taught me this technique to
bring someone back from the dead.

138
00:15:00,860 --> 00:15:04,290
Einar, speak to her as loudly as you can.

139
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:09,170
Arnheid, don't go!

140
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:16,300
I... I love you! I need you!

141
00:15:16,930 --> 00:15:19,930
I want you to laugh at my stories again!

142
00:15:19,930 --> 00:15:22,230
Please live!

143
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:25,540
Live with me again!

144
00:15:26,940 --> 00:15:30,480
Please live!

145
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:46,330
Einar, that's enough.

146
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,260
Far to the west...

147
00:16:51,890 --> 00:16:59,140
and across the sea,
there's a place called Vinland.

148
00:17:01,390 --> 00:17:04,800
Warm and bountiful, it is a distant land,

149
00:17:05,630 --> 00:17:11,430
beyond the reach of slave-traders
and the flames of war.

150
00:17:12,770 --> 00:17:18,600
You would be able to live
without suffering there.

151
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:22,740
Arnheid...

152
00:17:24,690 --> 00:17:28,120
Let's go there together.

153
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:33,280
Let's build a peaceful nation in Vinland.

154
00:17:57,630 --> 00:18:02,260
It's you guys. What are you still doing here?

155
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:12,770
Don't, Einar!

156
00:18:13,630 --> 00:18:15,020
Ketil!

157
00:18:16,620 --> 00:18:19,600
You! You killed Arnheid!

158
00:18:21,210 --> 00:18:24,720
I'll kill you. I'll fucking kill you!

159
00:18:26,660 --> 00:18:30,960
Don't, Einar! Killing the master
won't help anything!

160
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:39,590
I see. Arnheid is dead.

161
00:18:41,490 --> 00:18:43,340
Open your eyes, Einar!

162
00:18:43,800 --> 00:18:44,970
Please!

163
00:18:45,460 --> 00:18:46,720
Einar!

164
00:19:15,780 --> 00:19:23,270
Einar, killing the master
won't quell your rage.

165
00:19:25,410 --> 00:19:27,400
Anger begets more anger.

166
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:30,820
It just results in deaths, one after another.

167
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:37,610
I was stuck in that hell for a long time.

168
00:19:39,860 --> 00:19:42,680
Please, Einar.

169
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:47,520
Don't fall under the same curse
that afflicted me.

170
00:20:23,230 --> 00:20:24,210
Dad...

171
00:20:24,910 --> 00:20:28,360
I know. Get the ship ready to depart.

172
00:21:00,770 --> 00:21:07,250
God... must be watching us,
even as we stand here now.

173
00:21:14,430 --> 00:21:18,660
People losing friends, and parents
and children killing each other...

174
00:21:19,470 --> 00:21:25,510
He must be looking down on everything
from up high in heaven.

175
00:21:40,850 --> 00:21:41,920
Thorfinn...

176
00:21:42,810 --> 00:21:45,320
Wait. Where are you going?

177
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:48,320
Wait! What do you intend to do?

178
00:21:49,820 --> 00:21:52,320
I'm going to see Canute.

179
00:21:52,730 --> 00:21:53,430
What?

180
00:21:54,880 --> 00:21:58,470
The master is still alive.
He hasn't been captured.

181
00:21:59,030 --> 00:22:01,080
The battle isn't over.

182
00:22:02,450 --> 00:22:05,800
I may be able to prevent more deaths.

183
00:22:06,540 --> 00:22:09,490
That's ridiculous. We need to
leave this place immediately.

184
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:13,970
Why do you have to do this?

185
00:22:15,720 --> 00:22:16,470
Thorfinn!

186
00:22:24,540 --> 00:22:26,260
This time...

187
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:31,190
This time, please let me
take you back to Iceland.

188
00:22:32,990 --> 00:22:34,020
Please.

189
00:22:39,650 --> 00:22:43,960
Long ago, you once told me...

190
00:22:46,140 --> 00:22:55,720
that our ancestors fled from war
and ended up in Iceland.

191
00:22:58,140 --> 00:23:03,910
At the time, I thought it was lame,

192
00:23:05,200 --> 00:23:09,190
but now, I'm really proud of them.

193
00:23:10,270 --> 00:23:11,410
Thorfinn...

194
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:20,020
I'd estimate Canute
only brought around 100 men.

195
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:23,430
No matter how badly it turns out,

196
00:23:25,310 --> 00:23:28,710
I should be able to make it back alive.

197
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:44,690
We'll have the ship
ready to depart at any time.

198
00:23:45,380 --> 00:23:46,640
Don't push yourself too hard!

199
00:23:47,820 --> 00:23:53,660
We're going back to Iceland,
no matter what, Thorfinn!

200
00:25:36,260 --> 00:25:39,970
Courage

201
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:39,170
"Courage."
